-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",170,{
[5409]="7006559F\n1\tDefeat woods snipers (total: 8)\030Defeat forest prowlers (total: 4)\030Defeat a bandit captain\tIrzeben has asked you to defeat the growing bandit threat in the woods south of Furukzahar. The woods are in northern Lower Lebennin.\n2\tReturn to Irzeben\tYou should let Irzeben know that you have defeated many of the bandits in the forest south of Furukzahar. Irzeben is in the Zarsatrâd.\n",
[5410]="7004A8F1\n1\tBurn slain Orcs at Durthang in Lhingris (total: 8)\tSlain Orcs can be found littering the road leading to Durthang in Lhingris. You have noticed that burning the dead of Durthang has worked to repel the spiders of Lhingris. You should burn slain Orcs to fend off the spiders of Lhingris.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have burned many of the slain Orcs at the gates of Durthang in Lhingris.\n",
[5411]="70062DD7\n1\tDefeat foes within Caras Gelebren (total: 10)\tEnemies can be found throughout the ruins of Caras Gelebren.\n2\tTalk to Ilarion at Echad Terthas\tIlarion is at Echad Terthas.\n",
[5412]="7005A498\n1\tCollect poisoned arrows (total: 12)\030Defeat enemies at Rung-shakam (total: 12)\030Collect poison pouches (total: 4)\tRung-shakam is located in north-western Azanulbizar. You should collect poisoned arrows and poison pouches in Rung-shakam.\n2\tReturn to Edash\tEdash is located in Amdân. Bring the arrows and pouches to Edash.\n",
[5413]="7006B88D\n1\tDefeat Orc scouts (total: 8)\tUsing the information from the scouting report gathered from Irkiri, Galâmka has asked you to clear out Orc scouts in the area to the south-east to prevent them from finding the camp.\n2\tReturn to Galâmka in Ub Nishir\tReturn to Galâmka in Ub Nishir to the north of Maurûsh and inform him that you have eliminated the Orc scouts.\n",
[5414]="7003A663\n1\tFind the ford north of Flodgeheld\tThe winding Swiftwater River has a shallow ford north of Flodgeheld where the cliff walls dip down into steep but climbable banks along the river; however, they quickly rise up into a canyon just beyond that.\n2\tFind evidence of the White Hand's passing\tA footprint can be seen in the grass on the other side of the ford. It was likely made by the White Hand that were suspected to have come through here recently.\n3\tFind more evidence\tIt seems likely that more footprints were made which could help indicate which direction they went. You should search the land as it rises north of the river for more footprints.\n4\tFind more evidence\tThe grass grows thick as the ground rises from the river, and it may be harder to follow the trail of the White Hand. You will need to search for more evidence to determine which direction they went.\n5\tScout Mate Isernore\tThe party of White Hand that crossed the river appeared to lead in the direction of one of Gifemund's mines, Mate Isernore.\n6\tTalk to Herubrand\tHerubrand is in the cellar of the farmhouse in Woodhurst. You have much to tell Herubrand, with your efforts in Brockbridge, the situations in Flodgeheld and Madh-fushaum, and more recently what you found in Mate Isernore.\n",
[5415]="70071777\n1\tFind the footprints Rhadrog mentioned\tThough the gait of the tracks implies that they were not made by a soldier or bandit, Rhadrog is curious about who else may be roaming this barren land. He has asked you to take a look at the footprints for yourself, and he will assure Khagâmi's safety.\n2\tExamine the footprints\tYou have found the footprints of which Rhadrog spoke. You should follow them and see where they lead.\n3\tFollow the trail of footprints\tYou have found the footprints of which Rhadrog spoke. You should follow them and see where they lead.\n4\tTalk to Faeron\tYou have found the footprints of which Rhadrog spoke and followed them to this road. For some reason, Faeron is here? You should talk to Faeron.\n",
[5416]="70039F1D\n1\tLocate the boar-totem\tThane Sparhafoc wants you to search for this boar-totem in the swamps. Tova mentioned that it was just south-east of Fenmarch.\n2\tInvestigate the boar-totem\tYou have located the boar-totem in the swamps. Get a closer look and investigate the totem.\n3\tDefeat the attacking Orcs (total: 4)\tUpon investigating the boar totem, a group of Orcs attacks. Defeat the attacking Orcs.\n4\tTalk to Thane Sparhafoc\tThere is little doubt in your mind that the attacking Orcs are connected with the boar-totems found around Eastfold. Return to Thane Sparhafoc and inform him of your findings.\n",
[5417]="70032DDA\n1\tExamine the purity of the water in the Hall of Flowing Water\tWater can be tested at any of the waterfalls in the Hall of Flowing Water. You should use the phial to collect samples of water in Zelem-melek.\n2\tWater can be tested in the reservoirs in passages adjacent to the Hall of Flowing Water. You should use the phial to collect samples of water in Zelem-melek.\t\n3\tSearch near the Hall of Flowing Water for more water sources\tOther sources of water may be near the Hall of Flowing Water. You should search near the Hall of Flowing Water for more water sources to sample.\n4\tReturn to Búi with your findings\tBúi is in the Hall of Flowing Water in central Zelem-melek. You should return to Búi with your findings.\n",
[5418]="700529CE\n1\tTalk to Langhár\tLanghár can be summoned to your side with Langhár's summoning horn. You should talk to Langhár.\n2\tFind evidence of the attackers' identities\tThere should be some evidence near Ainhard's home that can confirm who the attackers were. You should find evidence of the attackers' identities.\n3\tInvestigate the tracks\tLanghár has identified goblin tracks near Ainhard's home. You should investigate the goblin tracks.\n4\tDefeat the ambushers\tWhile investigating the tracks outside Ainhard's home, you were ambushed by goblins! You should defeat the goblins.\n5\tExamine the scrap of paper\tThe goblin ambushers near Ainhard's home appear to have dropped a scrap of paper. You should examine the paper.\n6\tTalk to Langhár\tLanghár can be summoned to your side with Langhár's summoning horn. You should talk to Langhár.\n7\tTalk to Ainhard\tAinhard's Homestead lies south of Vegbár. in the Wolf-denes. You should talk to Ainhard.\n8\tHelp Ainhard with 'Hounds in the Woods'\030Help Langhár with 'Picking up the Pieces'\030Help Langhár with 'Lurking Looters'\tAinhard's Homestead lies south of Vegbár. in the Wolf-denes. You should complete quests to help Ainhard.\n9\tTalk to Ainhard\tAinhard's Homestead lies south of Vegbár. in the Wolf-denes. You should talk to Ainhard.\n10\tTalk to Langhár\tLanghár can be summoned to your side with Langhár's summoning horn. You should talk to Langhár.\n",
[5419]="70015E17\n1\tSearch camp-site for signs of the Company's passing\tThe camp-site lies east and north of Echad Eregion, beyond Torech Bornagol and Torech Carangor. Golgallon has asked you to search another camp-site for signs of the Company's passing.\n2\tTalk to Golgallon at Echad Eregion\tGolgallon is at Echad Eregion, west and south of the camp-site, beyond Torech Carangor and Torech Bornagol. You should return to Golgallon and warn him that the camp-site has been disturbed and something carried away.\n",
[5420]="7003766F\n1\tFollow the rivulet to see if it is safe\tThe rivulet running north to south in the Westfold branches west towards Helm's Deep. You should patrol the banks to see if this is a safe path for the refugees to follow, as the roads do not seem so promising.\n2\tFollow the rivulet southwards to see if it is safe\tThe rivulet running north to south in the Westfold branches west towards Helm's Deep. You should patrol the banks to see if this is a safe path for the refugees to follow, as the roads do not seem so promising.\n3\tContinue to follow the rivulet south-west\tThe rivulet running north to south in the Westfold branches west towards Helm's Deep. You should patrol the banks to see if this is a safe path for the refugees to follow, as the roads do not seem so promising.\n4\tContinue to follow the rivulet west\tThe rivulet running north to south in the Westfold branches west towards Helm's Deep. You should patrol the banks to see if this is a safe path for the refugees to follow, as the roads do not seem so promising.\n5\tCompleted\tYou have scouted the river, and it seems to be the safest route of all.\n",
[5421]="7005B229\n1\tExamine the supply area in Aslíf\tNáin has tasked you with tracking down the scout Múta, who was investigating missing supplies. Examining the supply area on the lower level of Aslíf should be the first step to solving this mystery.\n2\tYou have found scratch marks near the supply area in Aslíf. Following the scratch marks may help you find Múta.\t\n3\tTalk to Múta at Gabil-memâg\tYou have found Múta at Gabil-memâg. You should talk to her.\n",
[5422]="7002D4A2\n1\tTalk to Thalfar at his mining-camp\tThalfar is at the central mining-camp of the Silvertine Lodes, south from the Deep Descent camp. You should speak with Thalfar at his mining-camp.\n",
[5423]="7002D537\n1\tFind the hidden door in the southern passages\tSori mentioned a hidden door along the southern passages of the Silvertine Lodes that would help you follow the dwarf Öndótt. You should search the southern tunnel for the hidden door to the ancient dwarf-city.\n2\tFind Öndótt in the ancient city of the Silvertine\tÖndótt can be found in the ancient and abandoned dwarf-city of the Silvertine Lodes. You should find and speak with Öndótt.\n",
[5424]="70066E87\n1\tComplete 'Upokhir's Allies'\030Complete 'Rescue at Pahor Boha'\030Complete 'Scouting Pahor Boha'\tTorthril has asked you to help Upokhir and his allies within Pahor Boha. Pahor Boha can be found in the south-east of Pinnath Gelin.\n2\tTalk to Upokhir\tYou to have aided completed the tasks that Torthril and Upokhir have given you and should speak with them again. Upokhir and Torthril can be found at Ost Arndír.\n",
[5425]="70027100\n1\tTalk to Iestin at the Boar-clan encampment\030Collect food from Lhan Colvarn (total: 10)\tFood-stores can be found at Lhan Colvarn, north of the Boar-clan encampment. Iestin has asked you to gather food-stores for him.\n",
[5426]="7005AAC1\n1\tHelp injured dwarves (total: 6)\tInjured dwarves must be rescued from Borkordh, the drake nest on the south-east side of the Pit of Stonejaws.\n2\tTalk to Molkha outside Borkordh\tMolkha is scouting outside Borkordh.\n",
[5427]="70041786\n1\tUse the cooking pot to fill the bowls\tThe cooking pot can be found next to Siriel. You should use the cooking pot to fill the bowls with food.\n2\tHungry refugees can be found to the east of Siriel, near the shipyard. You should feed the nearby hungry refugees.\t\n3\tTalk to Siriel\tSiriel is located in the market east of Tol Ciryarani. You should speak with Siriel.\n",
[5428]="7000703C\n1\tSpeak with Mallennor\030Collect thick aurochs hides (total: 6)\030Collect aurochs meat (total: 6)\tAurochs can be found in Rhunenlad and Nan Amlug, east of Esteldín. Mallennor has been tasked with providing shelter and food for the Rangers of Esteldín and has asked you to help them by hunting aurochs for hide and meat.\n",
[5429]="7002C9AB\n1\tPlant seeds in fertile patches of land (total: 7)\tAn old, abandoned farmstead lies south along the River Limlight in Eorlsmead. You should plant the seeds Tatwine gave you at whatever fertile-seeming land you find in Eorlsmead.\n2\tReturn to Tatwine\tTatwine is at the stables in Stangard. You should return to Tatwine and tell him that you planted seeds and hope for a healthy harvest in the future.\n",
[5430]="70069441\n1\tComplete Umbar Cook's Guild daily orders (total: 5)\tComplete requests from the Umbar Cook's Guild. You can acquire these quests from the Umbar Cook's Guild Leader in the Umbar Baharbêl craft guild hall.\n2\tCompleted\tYou completed many Umbar cook requests.\n",
[5431]="7002720A\n1\tCollect food stores (total: 10)\tFood stores can be found throughout Upper Barnavon. Kai has asked you to collect food stores from the Ox-clan and distribute it among the Boar-clan.\n2\tStarving families can be found throughout Lower Barnavon. Kai asked you to distribute the food stores among the families of Lower Barnavon.\t\n3\tTalk to Kai in Barnavon\tKai is in Lower Barnavon. You should return to Kai and let him know that you have distributed the food as he had asked.\n",
[5432]="70045419\n1\tCollect porridge from the cauldron\tThe cauldron can be found in the War-stead of the Helmingas. You should collect porridge from the cauldron.\n2\tHungry Rohirrim can be found in the War-steads of the Helmingas and the King's Men. You should feed the hungry riders.\t\n3\tCompleted\tYou fed the hungry riders and restored some of their strength, as well as eased their appetites.\n",
[5433]="7005943A\n1\tCollect fish from fishing nets (total: 10)\tFishing nets can be found along the shores of the Brandywine, near Trader's Wharf. You should collect fish from fishing nets for the League of the Axe.\n2\tReturn to Grun Curldock with the fish you have collected\tGrun Curldock can be found at Trader's Wharf. You should return to Grun Curldock with the fish you have collected.\n",
[5434]="7003A477\n1\tFind the food stores\tThe food-supplies in Madh-fushaum are stored in sacks that are spread out throughout the camp. You should find them and destroy them.\n2\tFind the food-stores\tThe food-supplies in Madh-fushaum are stored in sacks that are spread out throughout the camp. You should find them and destroy them.\n3\tFind a torch\tThe food-supplies in Madh-fushaum are stored in sacks that are spread out throughout the camp. You should find them and destroy them.\n4\tDestroy food-supplies (total: 6)\tThe food-supplies in Madh-fushaum are stored in sacks that are spread out throughout the camp. You should find them and destroy them.\n5\tComplete\tDestroying the food-stores of this large army will have a devastating effect on its health and morale, unless the leaders of the army can find a new supply soon.\n",
[5435]="7002D505\n1\tFind grain in the area (total: 6)\tThe food for the food-trough can be found around the stable area.\n2\tReturn the grain to the trough\tThe grain can be placed in the food-trough inside the new horse's stall.\n",
[5436]="7000997F\n1\tDefeat the stone-giant chieftain\tThe stone-giant chieftain is at Amon Môth, south and west of the Eavespires. Remmenylf has asked you to defeat the stone-giant chieftain of Amon Môth.\n2\tTalk to Remmenylf at the Eavespires\tRemmenylf resides in the Eavespires, east and north of Amon Môth. You should return to Remmenylf and tell him of the chieftain's defeat.\n",
[5437]="700622F6\n1\tTalk to Haerlendir\tTham Celechir can be found north of Idhobel. Rhovandis has asked you to speak to Haerlendir just outside of Tham Celechir on the road.\n2\tLook for warg cages inside Tham Celechir\tThe scout has informed you that Uruk-hai have encamped within Tham Celechir. Be careful as you investigate the ruins.\n3\tTalk to Haerlendir\tYou found evidence of warg activity within Tham Celechir. Return to Haerlendir just outside of the ruins south of Tham Celechir.\n",
[5438]="7000874D\n1\tReturn to Dâr-gazag and speak with Chieftain Durulkum\030Collect footmen's badges (total: 10)\tSeek footmen, wardens, or scouts throughout the Ettenmoors and slay them. Chieftain Durulkum directed you to seek out the weakest of the enemy soldiers and claim their badges as proof of your duty.\n",
[5439]="70072F8D\n1\tScout north-east Adagím\030Scout eastern Adagím\030Scout south-east Adagím\tMálacál has asked that you travel to east of Sul Madásh, along the ridges, and scout the area for threats.\n2\tReturn to Málacál\tReturn to Málacál near Sul Madásh and report your findings after scouting eastern Adagím.\n",
[5440]="7005A692\n1\tCheck on the water-collection buckets\tYou should check on and collect melted snow from Dági's collection buckets. He placed the buckets at a snowy overlook to the south-east of Ashmargathâl, just off the road in Tharkh Shathur.\n2\tExamine the disturbed snow for tracks\tThe collection buckets have been tampered with. Checking the surrounding snow for clues may point you to the right direction.\n3\tTalk to Dági\tDági at Ashmargathâl will want to know about the Orc footprints you found.\n",
})
